OL,3,GNEWSAMinimum wage increase accepted by
OL,4,Aminister
OL,5,
OL,6,FA recommendation to increase the
OL,7,Fminimum wage has been accepted by the
OL,8,Fsocial security minister.
OL,10,Fb@KThe Jersey Employment Forum's latest
OL,11,Freport recommended hiking the minimum
OL,12,Fwage rate to #13.97 per hour from 1
OL,13,FApril 2027 - an increase of 2.8% on the
OL,14,Fcurrent #13.59 in line with the Jersey
OL,15,Fretail price index (RPI) in June 2026.
OL,17,FSenator Elaine Millar, Minister for
OL,18,FSocial Security, said she had "decided
OL,19,Fto accept the forum's recommendations
OL,20,Fin respect of the main minimum wage and
OL,21,Ftrainee minimum wage rates".
OL,23,APub: 29-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Ch Is NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
